cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss KYM, please cite it as below. KYM is an experimental proof of concept with synthetic data; it is not a standard."
title: "KYM (Know Your Mandate): a control plane and evidence ledger for financial authority delegated to AI agents"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-26
authors:
  - family-names: Clas
    given-names: Paul
repository-code: "https://github.com/PaulClas/Know-The-Mandate"
abstract: >-
  KYM is an experimental open proof of concept in which a fictional bank (Meridian Bank) represents a customer's
  delegated financial authority to an AI agent as a stateful, revocable mandate, evaluates it deterministically on
  every request even when the agent holds a valid OAuth token, and records the exercise of authority in a signed,
  hash-chained evidence ledger. It reuses OAuth 2.0 (PKCE, PAR, DPoP, RFC 9396), JSON-LD, SHACL, PROV-O and ODRL.
  Synthetic data only; sandbox security mechanisms; not certified or production-ready.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - agentic banking
  - delegated authority
  - mandate
  - OAuth
  - Rich Authorization Requests
  - DPoP
  - authorization
  - policy enforcement
  - evidence ledger
  - open banking
  - SHACL
  - JSON-LD
